.TH MVOLFORMAT 1.SH NAMEmvolformat \- format a numbered set of floppy disks.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmvolformat\fRdrive volname count [format options].SH DESCRIPTION\fBmvolformat\fRformats\fIcount\fRfloppies, from 1 to 99, one after another in\fIdrive\fR\fR(\fB/d0\fR),\fRnaming them\fIvolname\fRwith the number of each appended -- so a backup set comes out labelledin order.  It runs your system's\fBformat\fRfor each disk and passes on any of its options except\fB\-r\fRand\fB\-v\fR.\fRIt needs a floppy drive and your own OS-9's\fBformat\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOformat, dsave